{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PnAveragingUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PnAveragingUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_uniform_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_uniform_bar","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L249-L255","doc":"The uniform form is bar-invariant (existence half). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_unique","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L237-L247","doc":"**Uniqueness among constant coefficients.**  If `z − c·h` with a\nconstant `c` is bar-invariant at some `q` with `h(q) ≠ 0`, then\n`2c = 1`: the uniform form `z − h/2` is the only one.  This says\nnothing about a `q`-dependent `c`, such as the colour-weighted form. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pn-averaging-uniqueness","label":"prop:pn-averaging-uniqueness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_bar_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_bar_iff","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L226-L235","doc":"**Bar-invariance criterion.**  The averaging `z − c·h` takes the same\nvalue at `q` and `q⁻¹` iff `(c(q) + c(q⁻¹) − 1)·h(q) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pnZD_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pnZD_inv","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L210-L224","doc":"`z̄ = z − h` under convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pnH_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pnH_inv","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L207-L208","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pnH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pnH","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L204-L205","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pnZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pnZD","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L201-L202","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_unique_via_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pn_averaging_unique_via_weight","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L171-L189","doc":"**Uniqueness theorem (via the color-pair weight).**  Two p-n\naveragings sharing the same color-pair weight function `w` are\nequal — uniqueness follows from the 9-pair factorisation\nalone, independently of `StandardNorm`.\n\nThis is the **substantive content** of the refined\n`ColorFlavorCompatible` class: instead of pinning σ_{pn}\npointwise via a normalisation `z`, the class fixes the\nstructural form (the 9-pair decomposition with quark-type\nmultiplicities) and shifts the open math to selecting `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ninth_eq_ninth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ninth_eq_ninth","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L158-L169","doc":"The carried reciprocal of `9` is unique: any two `ColorFlavorCompatible`\ninstances over the same ring supply the same `ninth`.  (A two-sided\ninverse in a monoid is unique — this is the reason the R[h] carrying\nloses nothing relative to a field's `1/9`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.factors","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L152-L152","doc":"σ_{pn}(q) decomposes as the 9-pair weighted average across the\np-n boundary with the quark-type-pair multiplicities forced by\np = uud × n = udd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.ninth_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.ninth_spec","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L148-L148","doc":"…pinned by its defining multiplicative relation.  A two-sided\ninverse is unique, so `ninth` is determined by `R`, not chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.ninth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.ninth","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L145-L145","doc":"The reciprocal of the 9-pair count, carried as ring data (§7c\nR[h] pattern) rather than as a field division `1/9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.weight","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L142-L142","doc":"The per-pair color-tube weighting function.  Pinning this to\nthe canonical Bring color-tube form is the open math. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible.mk","kind":"ctor","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorFlavorCompatible","kind":"class","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L113-L156","doc":"**Color-flavor compatibility (refined predicate).**  σ_{pn}\nfactors through the 9-pair Bring color-tube decomposition\nacross the p-n boundary, with per-pair weights given by a\n`ColorPairWeight` function carried by the substrate.\n\nThe class field `weight` is the **open math entry point**:\nclosing it to the canonical Bring color-tube weighted form\nis the Phase 5q audit's load-bearing step.  The structural\ndecomposition `factors` is the substantive content this\nclass adds — the 2·(u,u) + 4·(u,d) + 1·(d,u) + 2·(d,d)\nquark-pair multiplicities arise from p = uud × n = udd.\n\n**Derivation-chain note (2026-05-30).**  The substrate\nevaluation `w(t, t', q) = 1/(1 − h_q · q^{10})` per\n`lambda_scale_refinement_h4_correction_bring.py` is not\npurely empirical: the `q^{10}` exponent is the residue/pole\norder of σ on the torus knot T(3,5), derived via\n`prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot` (`alphaShift p k = k·(p−1)`,\nLean-proved in `mass-theory/alpha-shift-torus-knot.lean`\nconditional on `HasAlphaShiftTorus 3 5`).  T(3,5) is the\nsecond member of the genus-4 force-carrier pair\n`{T(2,9), T(3,5)}` on Bring's surface\n(`prop:em-coupling-bring-zero-mode`, genus g = 4).  Thus the\n\"10\" in the closed-form Bring weight is derived; the\nremaining open math is the residue calculation giving the\nresolvent `1/(1 − ·)` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColorPairWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColorPairWeight","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L99-L111","doc":"A **color-pair weight** function: takes the quark types at the\npaired sheets across the p-n boundary and returns the\nsubstrate-q weighting factor.  Closing this function to the\ncanonical Bring color-tube form is the open math —\n`probe_pn_flavor_asymmetry.py` Scheme 4 PL integration on\nBring's surface gives the empirical recipe; the closed\nsubstrate form per\n`lambda_scale_refinement_h4_correction_bring.py` is\n`w(_, _, q) = 1 / (1 − h_q · q^{10})` at the substrate value\n(independent of the quark-type pair, modulo the higher-order\n`h_q^4` correction tracked in that probe). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprQuarkType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprQuarkType","kind":"instance","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprQuarkType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprQuarkType.repr","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqQuarkType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqQuarkType","kind":"instance","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuarkType.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuarkType.d","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuarkType.u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuarkType.u","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuarkType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuarkType","kind":"inductive","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L91-L97","doc":"Quark type at a color sheet — up or down.  Sufficient for the\np-n boundary decomposition; flavour generations / strange etc.\nare post-isospin extensions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvariant.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvariant.bar","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvariant.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvariant.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarInvariant","kind":"class","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L65-L73","doc":"**Bar-invariance.**  σ_{pn} is fixed under the substrate\nbar-involution q ↔ q⁻¹.  This is the structural floor that any\nHecke-algebra averaging functional respecting the Skein\nself-duality must satisfy.\n\nThe substrate parameter ranges over the **units** `Rˣ`, which over\na field is exactly the old `q ≠ 0` side condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PnAveragingForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PnAveragingForm","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-averaging-uniqueness.lean#L59-L63","doc":"A p-n interface averaging functional acts as a `q`-rational\nexpression: it takes the substrate parameter `q` and returns the\naveraging weight in the ground ring `R`.  Pre-Arch: `R`\nabstract; Archimedean realisation is post-τ. ","signatureChunk":0}]}